/Pg 15 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 294 0 R
/T (<b>Lamp</b></h2>\) break simple patterns. The parser tracks nesting depth: a container with class product, product-card or product-item opens a record, and child elements whose class contains name/title, price or rating supply its fields.)
/E (<b>Lamp</b></h2>\) break simple patterns. The parser tracks nesting depth: a container with class product, product-card or product-item opens a record, and child elements whose class contains name/title, price or rating supply its fields.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
662 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 294 0 R
/T (Regular expressions do the cleaning. Currency markers \(Rs, INR, $, the rupee sign\) and thousands separators are removed and the price is parsed as a Decimal, which must be above 0. The rating is the first number in the text, so 4.8 out of 5 and 4.7/5 both work, and it must lie between 0 and 5. HTML entities such as &amp; are decoded.)
/E (Regular expressions do the cleaning. Currency markers \(Rs, INR, $, the rupee sign\) and thousands separators are removed and the price is parsed as a Decimal, which must be above 0. The rating is the first number in the text, so 4.8 out of 5 and 4.7/5 both work, and it must lie between 0 and 5. HTML entities such as &amp; are decoded.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
663 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 294 0 R
/T (Duplicates: names are compared case-insensitively in a dictionary, and the better offer \(higher rating, then lower price\) is kept. A block with a missing or invalid field is skipped and counted.)
/E (Duplicates: names are compared case-insensitively in a dictionary, and the better offer \(higher rating, then lower price\) is kept. A block with a missing or invalid field is skipped and counted.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
664 0 obj
<<
