/T (stays exact\). p1 + p2 merges two records of the same product and raises an error for different ids. Inventory operators: a + b returns a new merged inventory without changing a or b \(shown in the test by reporting A after MERGE\); a += b merges in place; < and == compare total value, and @total_ordering supplies the other comparisons; len\(\), in, [] and iteration also work.)
/E (stays exact\). p1 + p2 merges two records of the same product and raises an error for different ids. Inventory operators: a + b returns a new merged inventory without changing a or b \(shown in the test by reporting A after MERGE\); a += b merges in place; < and == compare total value, and @total_ordering supplies the other comparisons; len\(\), in, [] and iteration also work.)
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
